  "prefLabel": "Ed 1004.01 Intention to Achieve an Employment Outcome",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1004.01 Intention to Achieve an Employment Outcome. During the application process, individuals shall be informed that vocational rehabilitation services are only provided if they intend to achieve an employment outcome as defined in 34 CFR 361.5(c)(15). Individuals with disabilities shall be active partners with the vocational rehabilitation counselor and together work to establish employment outcomes and the steps to reach those goals.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, #2, and #3 at chapter heading for Ed 1000) #13231, eff 7-13-21",
